+# cluster ci-d3e29f18fa53a626 — macos-x86_64 build: Qt 6-only `QStringList` fill constructor
+
+## Verdict
+
+FIXED. The hosted `macos-x86_64` build stopped at `tests/src/gui/MixerSendsOnFadersTest.cpp:278`
+(historical line) because the test built its expected fader list with
+`QStringList(channels, QStringLiteral("volume"))`. That two-argument fill constructor exists in Qt 6
+but not Qt 5.15, which the macOS job uses. The product answer was already correct; this was a
+test-source portability defect, not a behaviour defect.
+
+## Evidence
+
+- Failure from the pinned commit `fa4a5f2e785c73e32216931e33cdbe140c06647d` (this worktree's HEAD):
+  `QVERIFY(faders == QStringList(channels, QStringLiteral("volume")));` with
+  `error: no matching constructor for initialization of 'QStringList'` and candidates all requiring
+  one argument or an iterator pair.
+- Qt 5.15 header `/usr/include/qt/QtCore/qstringlist.h:115-121` lists only the default, `QString`,
+  `QList<QString>` copy/move, `initializer_list` and iterator-pair constructors — no `(count, value)`
+  fill constructor.
+- Qt 6 `qlist.h:311` adds `QList(qsizetype size, parameter_type t)`, which is why this compiled on
+  the Linux Qt 6 build and only failed on macOS/Qt 5.
+- The product contract itself is unchanged and correct:
+  `src/gui/ControlCommandsMixerView.cpp:64-73` (`faderRoles()`) emits one `"volume"` entry per channel
+  when no send is shown. The test's assertion (one `"volume"` per channel) is kept as-is; only the
+  way the expected list is built changed.
+- The old spelling is the only two-argument `QStringList` fill construction in the tree; the grep
+  used is recorded in the commands below.
+
+## Fix
+
+`tests/src/gui/MixerSendsOnFadersTest.cpp:276-281`: the expected list is built explicitly, one
+`QStringLiteral("volume")` per channel, then compared with the same `QVERIFY(faders == levels)`.
+The assertion is not weakened: it still requires every channel's drive to be `"volume"`. The
+comment records why the old spelling must not return.
+
+No product file, command, undo step, save format or audio-thread path changed. No new control
+command was added.
+
